Approach: Array Traversal

Create a new array ans with the same length as nums.

Iterate through every index i in nums.

Use nums[i] as an index to access another element in nums.

Store that value in ans[i] using ans[i] = nums[nums[i]].

Return the ans array.





















class Solution {
    publicint[] buildArray(int[] nums) {
        int[] ans = new int[nums.length];

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            ans[i] = nums[nums[i]];
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
